u}_e[1 - 2x_e(v + 1)]$ vanishes at $v_{\max} =  rac{1}{2x_e} - 1$. Substituting $v_{\max}$ into $	ilde{G}(v) = (v +  rac{1}{2})	ilde{
u}_e - (v +  rac{1}{2})^2	ilde{
u}_e x_e$ yields the well depth $D_e =  rac{	ilde{
u}_e}{4x_e}$ (whereas $D_0 = D_e - 	ilde{G}(0)$ is measured from $v = 0$). Hence, option (C) is correct.

Using $	ilde{
u}_{0 	o 1} = 	ilde{
u}_e(1 - 2x_e) = 2886	ext{ cm}^{-1}$ and $	ilde{
u}_{0 	o 2} = 2	ilde{
u}_e(1 - 3x_e) = 5668	ext{ cm}^{-1}$: $2	ilde{
u}_{0 	o 1} - 	ilde{
u}_{0 	o 2} = 2	ilde{
u}_e x_e = 5772 - 5668 = 104	ext{ cm}^{-1} \implies 	ilde{
u}_e x_e = 52	ext{ cm}^{-1}$. Then $	ilde{
u}_e = 2886 + 104 = 2990	ext{ cm}^{-1}$, giving $x_e =  rac{52}{2990} = 0.01739 \approx 0.0174$.
